{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And HaShem regretted.</b> It is known that He is not a man to regret; rather the Torah speaks in human language, for the Destroyer [of] what He had made will see both —" "And the sense of 'and it grieved Him to His heart' is the opposite of 'Let YHWH rejoice in His works' (Psalms 104:31), for it is good in His eyes that His creatures accept His kindnesses. And some say that 'and He regretted' is like 'comforts himself concerning you to kill you' (Genesis 27:42), and they explain it, and so said the Gaon [Saadia]. And they said that His heart is the prophet; and were it so, the word 'el' would not come after 'and it grieved.' And where do we find that a prophet is called 'heart'?"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:27.138712586Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}